    {
      "id": "MGL-03",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-finite-markings-integral-half-form",
      "title": "Which integral alternating form carries the markings?",
      "hypotheses": "A rational nondegenerate alternating form B adjoint for the order involution, a single positive rational scale s₁ with M self-dual at p for s₁B, and a unit ε away from p comparing s₁B through r with the reference integral form. Use the compatible markings of MGL-02.",
      "statement": "The half-form E=s₁B|L is integral and perfect over ℤ_(p), with an integer prime to p annihilating its integral cokernel. The full form is 2E. At every positive level prime to p, the lifted forms scale by the compatible residues of ε independently of the parity of the level.",
